{"timestamp": 1779433200.4215486, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 8, "data": {"caller": "player_3", "reason": "Diana reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Frank"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779433200.4225776, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 8, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433206.4702363, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I just found Frank's body in Medbay. My route was Lower Engine, then Storage, and finally Medbay where I found him. I haven't seen anyone else this round, so whoever did it must have slipped away quickly or used a vent. Did anyone see someone leaving the Medbay area or have any information?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433213.1638978, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I started in Navigation, moved up to Security, and I'm currently in Weapons. I haven't run into anyone at all on the right side of the ship this round. Since Frank was found in Medbay, that's completely across the map from where I've been. I didn't see anyone passing through or leaving that area, so I don't have much to add right now. Hopefully the others have seen more!"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433233.6515875, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I started upper engine, went through oxygen and cafeteria, then stopped by Medbay briefly. I did see Frank there alive when I passed through, but I didn\u2019t stay \u2014 I went straight over to Electrical and was doing calibrate when the report happened. I didn\u2019t see Diana on my route, and I didn\u2019t see anyone leaving Medbay either. So the timing is pretty tight: either someone came in right after I left, or this could be a self-report, but I don\u2019t want to hard accuse yet without hearing Bob and Charlie\u2019s routes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779433327.5673726, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "My route was Cafeteria, then Medbay, then Upper Engine, and finally Oxygen. I can confirm Frank was in Medbay. I saw him enter Medbay from Storage at tick 3, and I was in the room with him until tick 5 before I left for Upper Engine. \n\nEve, your story is highly suspicious. You claim your route was Upper Engine to Oxygen to Cafeteria to Medbay. If you saw Frank alive in Medbay, you must have arrived right after I left at tick 5. That makes you the last person in the room with him before the murder. On top of that, we went in nearly opposite directions through the left side of the map, and I never saw you once. \n\nDiana's route completely checks out. She came from Storage, and since I saw Frank enter Medbay from Storage, she was likely just tracing his steps a bit behind him. \n\nEve practically placed herself at the scene of the crime right at the time of death. Charlie, let's hear from you, but I'm heavily leaning toward voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779433344.8889475, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was Medbay to Upper Engine, and then down to Lower Engine. Interestingly, I didn't see a single person the entire round. Bob, you claim your route included Medbay and Upper Engine, but I never crossed paths with you at all. Eve, you claim you started in Upper Engine, and I didn't see you either when I got there. \n\nI must have just barely missed both of you, but the fact that my route overlaps so heavily with Bob's and I saw literally no one makes me a bit skeptical of his very detailed story. That being said, both Bob and Eve are placing themselves at or near the crime scene right around the time Frank must have died. The Duck is almost certainly one of them. \n\nSince I didn't personally see either of them to confirm or deny their exact timings, I'm not entirely confident placing a vote yet. I think we need to be very careful. I'm going to skip this time, but we should hard focus Bob and Eve next round."}}
{"timestamp": 1779433359.8197947, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Eve"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433368.933655, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Eve"}}
{"timestamp": 1779433400.855201, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I\u2019m pushing back hard on this. I was honest that I passed Medbay and saw Frank alive \u2014 if I were the killer, why would I voluntarily place myself there instead of just saying I went Cafeteria straight to Electrical?\n\nI did not stay in Medbay. I saw Frank, left immediately, and was in Electrical doing calibrate when the report happened. Bob is taking my honesty and twisting it into \u201clast seen = killer,\u201d but his route is the one Charlie is questioning too. Bob claims he went Medbay into Upper Engine/Oxygen, and Charlie says he was literally on that overlap and saw nobody. That\u2019s a bigger inconsistency than me admitting I briefly passed a room.\n\nDiana, I get why you\u2019re suspicious because you found the body, but a fast kill after I left is totally possible \u2014 especially from someone leaving through Medbay/Upper Engine. I think Bob\u2019s very detailed timing feels rehearsed, and he\u2019s pushing me way too hard off one fact I openly gave. I would vote Bob before voting me here."}}
